      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As someone who's an avid RTS player, i  have experienced games running dozens upon dozens, perhaps even hundreds of simultaneous audio sources, using culling systems that check based on volume and/or distance, as well as the priority bias specified per sound, (they also combine same sounds to make a louder sound instead of 3 sounds overlapping at the same time for performance), and either play them straight through channels or pre-mix them for a single channel output, but this has been present in games since the 90s - why does vrchat lack this simple fundamental feature?  If vrchat had this, then hard limiting sources would be pointless.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
